WEBVTT

00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:45.710
GRUMBLE RUMBLE

00:01:39.220 --> 00:01:40.640
Good morning!

00:01:41.010 --> 00:01:42.770
Welcome to Wagnaria!

00:01:43.220 --> 00:01:44.730
Table for one?

00:01:44.980 --> 00:01:46.730
Um, excuse me...

00:01:47.020 --> 00:01:48.020
Yes?

00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:51.190
I'm here for a part-time job interview.

00:01:51.940 --> 00:01:53.360
You're the one then.

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:55.450
I'm Higashida.

00:01:55.070 --> 00:01:57.070
DAISUKE HIGASHIDA

00:01:57.240 --> 00:02:00.120
I'll confirm with the manager,

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:03.540
so could you wait here for a moment?

00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:04.500
Sure.

00:02:09.790 --> 00:02:12.000
They do a good job
attending to customers,

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:14.800
and it seems like a decent restaurant.

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:23.560
I really don't want to work.

00:02:25.020 --> 00:02:28.230
OFFICE

00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:30.440
PART-TIME JOBS CAN CHANGE LIVES

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:29.350
Well, please have a seat there.

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:35.150
KENICHIROU SAKAKI

00:02:32.150 --> 00:02:33.980
I'm the manager, Sakaki.

00:02:36.740 --> 00:02:38.530
It's nice to meet you.

00:02:39.160 --> 00:02:42.700
Daisuke Higashida,
first-year high school student...

00:02:42.700 --> 00:02:45.950
Huh? This school prepares students
for university, doesn't it?

00:02:45.950 --> 00:02:49.170
Yes, I suppose.

00:02:49.710 --> 00:02:52.130
Wouldn't it be difficult
to work here and study?

00:02:52.130 --> 00:02:55.960
Well... I enjoy studying,
relatively speaking, so...

00:02:55.960 --> 00:02:58.430
Really! That's great.

00:02:58.430 --> 00:03:00.840
Um, okay, why are you looking
for a part-time job?

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:07.100
Minor motivation is completely fine.

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:09.770
My father's company went bankrupt.

00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:12.980
<i>That's major!</i>

00:03:14.020 --> 00:03:15.440
Mom, another helping.

00:03:15.690 --> 00:03:16.940
Okay, okay.

00:03:18.190 --> 00:03:19.570
Oh, that's right, everyone.

00:03:20.740 --> 00:03:22.030
Actually...

00:03:22.240 --> 00:03:25.660
KOUSAKU HIGASHIDA

00:03:22.990 --> 00:03:24.330
my business...

00:03:24.580 --> 00:03:25.660
has gone out of business.

00:03:26.330 --> 00:03:27.540
A corny gag?

00:03:27.790 --> 00:03:30.750
Y-You mean bankrupt, Dad?

00:03:30.750 --> 00:03:33.750
SAKIKO HIGASHIDA             SACHIKO HIGASHIDA

00:03:31.290 --> 00:03:34.000
Well, it can't be helped, right, dear?

00:03:34.250 --> 00:03:35.840
Businesses go out of business.

00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:37.260
That's right, Dad.

00:03:37.630 --> 00:03:40.220
Don't let a little bankruptcy
get you down.

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:45.560
Dad's business...

00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:46.640
...went out of business!

00:03:47.850 --> 00:03:49.020
Oh, dear...

00:03:50.600 --> 00:03:52.350
I worked on that gag.

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:54.810
What's wrong with you people?!

00:03:54.810 --> 00:03:55.860
Okay, calm down.

00:03:56.440 --> 00:03:58.570
I already know what my next job is.

00:03:59.150 --> 00:04:00.200
Oh...

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:01.360
Oh!

00:04:02.780 --> 00:04:06.240
I should warn you
that I'm taking a pay cut.

00:04:06.580 --> 00:04:09.410
Therefore, starting next month,
I can't pay you an allowance

00:04:09.410 --> 00:04:12.210
or take care of your phone bill,
so you'd better get a job.

00:04:12.670 --> 00:04:14.250
<i>I just got laid off?</i>

00:04:18.420 --> 00:04:21.300
<i>This school doesn't even allow
the students to work part-time.</i>

00:04:21.550 --> 00:04:22.720
Higashida!

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:25.300
Sensei, good morning.

00:04:25.970 --> 00:04:27.760
You're an admirable young man.

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:32.140
I hear you volunteered to get
a part-time job to help your family.

00:04:32.140 --> 00:04:32.890
Wrong!

00:04:32.890 --> 00:04:34.230
Your father called.

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:36.610
- I can explain—
- So I gave permission.

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:38.270
Good luck!

00:04:38.270 --> 00:04:39.900
Sensei!

00:04:40.860 --> 00:04:43.740
So I lost my allowance,
money for my phone bill

00:04:43.740 --> 00:04:46.280
and even money for my train pass.

00:04:46.740 --> 00:04:50.660
Without a pass,
it's 15 km to school by bicycle.

00:04:51.450 --> 00:04:55.630
To be honest, my grades will suffer,
so I don't want to work,

00:04:55.880 --> 00:04:58.130
but this place is close. What can I...

00:04:58.130 --> 00:05:00.920
I get it! I'll give you the job! Okay?

00:05:01.760 --> 00:05:03.840
Well, I look forward to working
with you starting today.

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:06.050
I look forward to working with you.

00:05:06.550 --> 00:05:08.760
This is Miyakoshi, the floor chief.

00:05:09.100 --> 00:05:10.390
She's also a high school student,

00:05:10.020 --> 00:05:12.810
HANA MIYAKOSHI

00:05:10.640 --> 00:05:12.810
so if you have any questions
about the job, just ask her.

00:05:13.310 --> 00:05:15.270
Nice to meet you.

00:05:15.520 --> 00:05:17.230
<i>She was here
when I came for my interview.</i>

00:05:17.230 --> 00:05:18.400
All right, let's get started.

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:19.320
Okay.

00:05:19.320 --> 00:05:21.650
First, about punching the manager...

00:05:21.650 --> 00:05:22.360
Huh?

00:05:22.780 --> 00:05:24.240
He's got a glass jaw.

00:05:24.240 --> 00:05:25.450
Miyakoshi!

00:05:25.450 --> 00:05:27.450
When a customer comes in,
you say "Welcome."

00:05:27.910 --> 00:05:31.450
In a loud voice. And when they leave,
you say, "Thank you for coming."

00:05:31.450 --> 00:05:32.290
Right.

00:05:32.290 --> 00:05:35.000
And after the customer leaves,
you clear the table right away.

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:35.830
Right.

00:05:35.830 --> 00:05:37.460
And then a right to the manager's jaw!

00:05:37.710 --> 00:05:39.920
You don't feed stray cats
near the restaurant!

00:05:39.920 --> 00:05:40.920
I-I'm sorry.

00:05:40.920 --> 00:05:49.640
MEN'S CHANGING ROOM

00:05:41.550 --> 00:05:43.340
That's about it for newbies.

00:05:43.670 --> 00:05:45.300
If there's something you don't get, ask.

00:05:45.300 --> 00:05:46.680
- Um...
- What?

00:05:46.680 --> 00:05:48.680
Am I required to do that last part?

00:05:50.560 --> 00:05:53.520
If you can't learn all this in a month,
that's gonna be you.

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:54.600
I'll be careful.

00:05:54.980 --> 00:05:57.020
All right, let's hit the floor.

00:05:57.350 --> 00:05:58.270
<i>She's scary.</i>

00:05:59.730 --> 00:06:02.360
<i>Why is someone like this a waitress?</i>

00:06:06.360 --> 00:06:08.410
Welcome!

00:06:08.660 --> 00:06:11.160
<i>I don't believe it!
Even her expression changed!</i>

00:06:12.740 --> 00:06:14.120
Thank you for coming.

00:06:14.830 --> 00:06:19.330
<i>But why is Miyakoshi so cruel
to the manager?</i>

00:06:19.580 --> 00:06:20.670
A receipt?

00:06:20.670 --> 00:06:23.340
<i>Certainly, you don't want stray cats
near the restaurant, but...</i>

00:06:23.710 --> 00:06:26.590
Nipopo Soccer Boy Scouts...

00:06:27.930 --> 00:06:29.090
Higashida!

00:06:29.340 --> 00:06:30.260
Yes, sir!

00:06:30.510 --> 00:06:33.060
How do you spell "scouts"?

00:06:33.430 --> 00:06:34.470
"Scouts"?

00:06:33.430 --> 00:06:34.470
SCOUTS

00:06:35.850 --> 00:06:37.640
- Thank you for coming.
- Thank you for coming.

00:06:38.230 --> 00:06:42.770
I knew you were smart, Higashida,
going to a good high school like that.

00:06:44.360 --> 00:06:46.070
<i>Is he...</i>

00:06:46.320 --> 00:06:48.240
<i>But maybe he just forgot.</i>

00:06:49.490 --> 00:06:52.030
Manager, what's 8 times 7?

00:06:52.280 --> 00:06:52.950
<i>Easy.</i>

00:06:56.370 --> 00:06:57.540
59!

00:06:57.790 --> 00:07:00.420
<i>Civilization's convenient device
wasn't any help!</i>

00:07:02.250 --> 00:07:04.130
Guess I'll do the back next.

00:07:07.220 --> 00:07:09.380
I started working here today.
I'm Higashida.

00:07:09.840 --> 00:07:12.350
SAYURI MURANUSHI

00:07:10.010 --> 00:07:11.720
I'm Sayuri Muranushi.

00:07:13.050 --> 00:07:14.510
Nice to meet you.

00:07:14.760 --> 00:07:16.100
Same here.

00:07:22.110 --> 00:07:23.440
Welcome.

00:07:24.900 --> 00:07:27.190
Table for one?

00:07:27.490 --> 00:07:28.650
Right this way.

00:07:29.530 --> 00:07:31.110
Here's our menu.

00:07:31.740 --> 00:07:33.320
Thank you for your patience.

00:07:33.740 --> 00:07:35.080
May I take your order?

00:07:37.290 --> 00:07:38.830
One coffee.

00:07:40.670 --> 00:07:42.630
The usual, black, right?

00:07:45.090 --> 00:07:46.090
Right away.

00:07:48.420 --> 00:07:50.090
M-Muranushi...

00:07:50.340 --> 00:07:52.010
- Yes?
- Um...

00:07:52.590 --> 00:07:54.760
Where is the customer?

00:07:55.640 --> 00:07:56.970
Maybe you didn't know.

00:07:57.270 --> 00:07:59.850
That elderly fellow is a regular here.

00:08:01.140 --> 00:08:04.610
He gets mad if you put milk
in his coffee, so be careful.

00:08:05.770 --> 00:08:07.230
Elderly fellow?

00:08:11.610 --> 00:08:12.660
Muranushi?

00:08:12.990 --> 00:08:14.530
She's normal as far as I know.

00:08:14.780 --> 00:08:16.280
If I had to come up with something...

00:08:16.950 --> 00:08:18.870
<i>You need to turn the heat on!</i>

00:08:18.870 --> 00:08:20.120
<i>It is on!</i>

00:08:20.120 --> 00:08:23.000
When she took off work
to take a college entrance exam,

00:08:23.000 --> 00:08:25.500
the restaurant was strangely
cold and dark...

00:08:25.500 --> 00:08:29.960
GET ME MURANUSHI

00:08:25.880 --> 00:08:29.960
and "Get me Muranushi" was written
in blood on the bathroom wall.

00:08:30.920 --> 00:08:32.800
But nothing really surprising happened.

00:08:32.800 --> 00:08:35.550
Your fearlessness surprises me.

00:08:36.010 --> 00:08:45.310
LETTUCE

00:08:36.300 --> 00:08:38.100
What are you talking about?

00:08:38.600 --> 00:08:40.230
Oh, Muranushi.

00:08:40.770 --> 00:08:43.850
Nice. Looks like you two
high schoolers are having fun.

00:08:43.850 --> 00:08:45.310
No, listen, Higashida...

00:08:46.610 --> 00:08:51.150
I noticed that you have the ability
to sense the supernatural.

00:08:51.440 --> 00:08:55.030
I don't believe in ghosts.
After all, I've never seen one.

00:08:55.450 --> 00:08:56.700
What?!

00:09:00.410 --> 00:09:02.120
What's with this place?

00:09:02.620 --> 00:09:04.080
The manager, the employees...

00:09:04.790 --> 00:09:06.540
The employees...

00:09:09.460 --> 00:09:11.970
What? You got a problem?

00:09:15.260 --> 00:09:18.930
This is Higashida.
He just started working here today.

00:09:19.390 --> 00:09:22.390
KISAKI KONDOU

00:09:19.680 --> 00:09:21.730
This is Kisaki Kondou.

00:09:21.730 --> 00:09:23.310
Nice to meet you.

00:09:24.640 --> 00:09:26.600
Um... Kisaki...

00:09:27.150 --> 00:09:29.520
your shift is about to start.

00:09:31.320 --> 00:09:33.610
U-Um, Kisaki...

00:09:34.780 --> 00:09:36.660
- I feel sluggish.
- Sluggish?!

00:09:36.910 --> 00:09:40.490
If the customers know there's
an exhausted employee working here,

00:09:40.490 --> 00:09:42.830
it looks bad for the restaurant.

00:09:42.830 --> 00:09:45.540
So I'm gonna rest a little more
for the restaurant's sake.

00:09:45.540 --> 00:09:46.330
I see!

00:09:46.920 --> 00:09:48.250
That makes sense.

00:09:48.250 --> 00:09:49.790
<i>What is this?</i>

00:09:50.170 --> 00:09:52.170
Knock it off, Kisaki!

00:09:52.170 --> 00:09:55.760
You don't work, you smoke!
Are you sure you wanna be here?

00:09:56.010 --> 00:09:57.010
Miyakoshi...

00:09:57.970 --> 00:09:59.930
What year was the Taika Reform?

00:10:04.640 --> 00:10:06.600
Th-That's not fair!

00:10:06.600 --> 00:10:08.810
Teasing me because you go
to a good university!

00:10:10.610 --> 00:10:14.820
Um, Kisaki, like Miyakoshi said,
you should be a little more—

00:10:14.820 --> 00:10:17.160
Higashida, you go
to a college prep high school?

00:10:17.160 --> 00:10:18.820
Yes, you're right.

00:10:19.070 --> 00:10:22.490
In the middle period of the Edo era,
under Yoshimune Tokugawa's orders,

00:10:22.490 --> 00:10:24.450
there were two scholars
who studied Dutch.

00:10:24.700 --> 00:10:27.210
Genjo Noro and Konyo Aoki.

00:10:29.290 --> 00:10:33.920
Come on. We're getting paid
an hourly wage, so let's get to work.

00:10:34.210 --> 00:10:36.050
That was cool, Higashida!

00:10:41.550 --> 00:10:45.430
I take the fulfilled order
from the counter and carry it...

00:10:45.930 --> 00:10:49.190
The person who's got the floor
is in charge of pouring the coffee.

00:10:49.190 --> 00:10:50.190
That.

00:10:50.860 --> 00:10:51.650
Understood.

00:10:52.610 --> 00:10:55.530
MASAHIRO ADACHI

00:10:52.860 --> 00:10:55.530
I'm Adachi, in charge of the kitchen.

00:10:55.860 --> 00:10:59.490
I'm Kouno. Good to meet you, newbie.

00:10:56.610 --> 00:10:59.490
TAKUYA KOUNO

00:10:59.860 --> 00:11:01.120
I'm Higashida.

00:11:01.370 --> 00:11:02.830
It's nice to meet you.

00:11:03.370 --> 00:11:05.040
Kouno, make a parfait!

00:11:05.040 --> 00:11:06.160
Roger!

00:11:06.450 --> 00:11:08.420
The person in charge of the floor
pours coffee.

00:11:08.420 --> 00:11:09.960
The kitchen handles desserts.

00:11:10.210 --> 00:11:14.090
Well, at a normal restaurant,
the person on the floor does parfaits.

00:11:14.090 --> 00:11:15.340
But we're special.

00:11:15.960 --> 00:11:16.800
Special?

00:11:16.970 --> 00:11:18.130
Kouno!

00:11:18.880 --> 00:11:19.680
Sorry!

00:11:19.680 --> 00:11:21.930
Nothing! Well, good luck!

00:11:22.760 --> 00:11:23.680
Higashida!

00:11:24.140 --> 00:11:26.220
It's your first day, so you don't have to
interact with the customers.

00:11:26.220 --> 00:11:27.770
Watch someone else
to see how it's done.

00:11:27.770 --> 00:11:29.140
Excuse me!

00:11:29.810 --> 00:11:32.610
This coffee is weaker than before!

00:11:32.860 --> 00:11:34.360
My apologies.

00:11:34.650 --> 00:11:36.650
What are you grinning about?

00:11:36.650 --> 00:11:39.530
Why don't you try showing me
a little sincerity?

00:11:41.950 --> 00:11:43.660
SINCERITY

00:11:43.990 --> 00:11:46.290
I apologize for the inconvenience.

00:11:47.370 --> 00:11:48.870
Come here, Kamakura!

00:11:50.370 --> 00:11:52.580
Kamakura, what do you think
the customers are?

00:11:52.790 --> 00:11:55.590
SHIHO KAMAKURA

00:11:53.840 --> 00:11:55.590
What do I think?
The ignorant masses?

00:11:57.090 --> 00:11:59.170
But I guess I apologize.

00:11:59.170 --> 00:12:01.760
Shiho has made Miyakoshi mad.

00:12:01.760 --> 00:12:03.050
Keep your money to yourself!

00:12:03.470 --> 00:12:04.720
That's enough, Kamakura.

00:12:05.220 --> 00:12:07.310
Quit looking down on us.

00:12:07.310 --> 00:12:08.350
Kisaki...

00:12:09.020 --> 00:12:10.140
That's not enough.

00:12:11.520 --> 00:12:13.980
What was I thinking? You're right.

00:12:14.560 --> 00:12:16.980
All of these people are scary
in their own way.

00:12:17.530 --> 00:12:20.150
She's the daughter
of a company president.

00:12:21.320 --> 00:12:22.990
Higashida, is it?

00:12:22.570 --> 00:12:25.160
YUUTA SHINDOU

00:12:23.740 --> 00:12:25.160
I'm Yuuta Shindou.

00:12:26.370 --> 00:12:27.870
It's nice to meet you.

00:12:28.200 --> 00:12:30.120
The manager told me about you.

00:12:30.370 --> 00:12:32.580
Sounds like you've got it rough, too.

00:12:32.580 --> 00:12:33.540
Yeah, well...

00:12:34.000 --> 00:12:36.800
It's complicated for me, too.
I deliver newspapers,

00:12:36.800 --> 00:12:40.510
work at a convenience store,
work here and at a male host club.

00:12:40.670 --> 00:12:42.050
Really?

00:12:42.050 --> 00:12:45.010
It's because my dad is in debt.

00:12:47.390 --> 00:12:49.140
To her dad!

00:12:50.060 --> 00:12:51.350
Okay, this much?

00:12:51.600 --> 00:12:52.940
- Yeah.
- Kisaki!

00:12:53.730 --> 00:12:56.110
It does sound rough
for you too, Shindou.

00:12:56.110 --> 00:12:57.320
Yeah, well...

00:12:57.320 --> 00:13:01.110
But at night, don't you get paid more
at the host club than here?

00:13:01.400 --> 00:13:04.610
No, this job is the most important
of them all.

00:13:04.610 --> 00:13:05.530
Important?

00:13:05.530 --> 00:13:06.370
Shindou...

00:13:07.700 --> 00:13:08.620
Here.

00:13:08.870 --> 00:13:11.040
Leftovers. Good through the end
of the day.

00:13:11.710 --> 00:13:15.040
The fair is over, so we've got
leftover frozen food, too.

00:13:15.040 --> 00:13:19.500
CHUCKLE CHUCKLE CHUCKLE CHUCKLE

00:13:15.580 --> 00:13:17.340
Thank you so much!

00:13:17.590 --> 00:13:19.500
We're really not supposed
to do this, though.

00:13:20.010 --> 00:13:21.920
But it would be a waste
to just throw it away.

00:13:22.470 --> 00:13:24.760
Everyone takes my money away.

00:13:25.220 --> 00:13:27.140
<i>P-Poor guy!</i>

00:13:27.510 --> 00:13:30.470
Um, is the debt
from an independent business?

00:13:31.180 --> 00:13:32.680
A butcher's shop.

00:13:32.930 --> 00:13:34.940
It could be torn down at any time,

00:13:35.190 --> 00:13:36.690
so I always carry a picture with me.

00:13:36.690 --> 00:13:38.650
SHINDOU BUTCHER SHOP

00:13:40.900 --> 00:13:41.860
That sign, right?

00:13:42.110 --> 00:13:43.450
It's the sign.

00:13:44.450 --> 00:13:48.160
But considering it's a butcher shop,
that might be proper in a way.

00:13:48.530 --> 00:13:49.370
What?

00:13:49.620 --> 00:13:51.120
- Yuuta...
- Yes?

00:13:51.790 --> 00:13:54.790
<i>The son of a man in debt...</i>

00:13:55.290 --> 00:13:59.170
GRIN GRIN GRIN GRIN

00:13:55.750 --> 00:13:58.000
<i>...and the daughter of the creditor.</i>

00:13:58.420 --> 00:13:59.170
Gimme your hand.

00:14:00.960 --> 00:14:02.460
Shindou! Shindou!

00:14:04.720 --> 00:14:09.260
Why is Kamakura even working
when she's a rich girl?

00:14:10.430 --> 00:14:12.640
That's because of when I was a kid...

00:14:12.890 --> 00:14:14.390
When you were a kid?

00:14:15.020 --> 00:14:17.100
It might be because I rejected Shiho.

00:14:18.480 --> 00:14:19.860
What do you mean?

00:14:21.440 --> 00:14:22.610
I'm home.

00:14:22.980 --> 00:14:24.070
I'm beat.

00:14:26.150 --> 00:14:30.950
It seems like the guys in the kitchen
are the only normal people there.

00:14:31.200 --> 00:14:32.290
Hey, Daisuke.

00:14:33.040 --> 00:14:34.790
Do you think the job will work out?

00:14:35.210 --> 00:14:37.000
I have no choice
but to hang in there, right?

00:14:37.370 --> 00:14:40.170
I have to do my best
and not give up either...

00:14:40.500 --> 00:14:41.710
on finding a job.

00:14:42.090 --> 00:14:45.630
Oh, honey, you already found
your next job, didn't you?

00:14:45.920 --> 00:14:47.050
That's right!

00:14:48.680 --> 00:14:50.050
Oh, that's right!

00:14:51.100 --> 00:14:52.810
It slipped my mind!

00:14:52.260 --> 00:14:53.520
<i>You people...</i>

00:14:56.140 --> 00:14:58.440
The crowd has finally thinned out.

00:14:58.690 --> 00:15:00.190
You're doing well, Higashida.

00:15:00.520 --> 00:15:02.650
It's tiring until you get used to it, huh?

00:15:02.900 --> 00:15:06.400
Although it's more relaxing
to work here

00:15:06.650 --> 00:15:08.950
than having to face
those nitwits at home.

00:15:09.280 --> 00:15:10.320
Nitwits?

00:15:10.320 --> 00:15:11.990
Oh, nothing.

00:15:14.040 --> 00:15:15.910
Oh, Daisuke!

00:15:15.910 --> 00:15:18.120
GRIMACE

00:15:18.460 --> 00:15:20.670
It's embarrassing
to have you here, so go home!

00:15:21.880 --> 00:15:25.630
Even if it's a lie, you should've said
that you're really busy, Daisuke.

00:15:26.010 --> 00:15:29.380
Given present circumstances,
how can we afford to eat out?

00:15:29.840 --> 00:15:32.470
We can figure something out, right?

00:15:32.720 --> 00:15:35.470
That's right.
You worry too much, Big Bro.

00:15:39.890 --> 00:15:40.810
Go home!

00:15:41.270 --> 00:15:43.730
Welcome!

00:15:44.730 --> 00:15:47.280
So you're Higashida's family?

00:15:47.280 --> 00:15:49.400
He works so hard.

00:15:49.650 --> 00:15:52.320
Oh, I'm just grateful he got a job here.

00:15:53.620 --> 00:15:56.750
Hamburg steak? Understood.

00:15:57.500 --> 00:15:59.080
It'll be a few minutes.

00:16:00.830 --> 00:16:01.960
Muranushi...

00:16:01.960 --> 00:16:03.290
Oh, Higashida.

00:16:03.540 --> 00:16:04.710
You've rallied 'round.

00:16:05.210 --> 00:16:08.970
Did my family say anything weird?

00:16:09.720 --> 00:16:12.720
Not that I heard... let's say.

00:16:13.640 --> 00:16:15.970
Wait! What does that mean?

00:16:16.220 --> 00:16:17.470
Muranushi!

00:16:17.720 --> 00:16:19.980
GRIMACE

00:16:21.900 --> 00:16:23.440
Check please, sir!

00:16:26.520 --> 00:16:27.610
Daisuke...

00:16:27.860 --> 00:16:31.650
even though we're your family, we're
customers here, and you're the employee.

00:16:32.160 --> 00:16:34.570
Make that distinction
and do your job right!

00:16:34.990 --> 00:16:37.490
<i>The one time he says
something serious...</i>

00:16:40.120 --> 00:16:41.920
Thank you.

00:16:41.920 --> 00:16:44.000
That'll be 8,280 yen.

00:16:44.420 --> 00:16:45.500
Fine.

00:16:49.760 --> 00:16:54.260
Daisuke, I forgot to bring money,
so pay this time, huh?

00:16:56.680 --> 00:16:58.470
<i>What happened
to making that distinction?</i>

00:17:00.180 --> 00:17:03.060
It looks like you've gotten used
to the job already, Higashida.

00:17:03.310 --> 00:17:05.810
Well, it has been two weeks.

00:17:06.060 --> 00:17:07.480
February already, huh?

00:17:08.110 --> 00:17:09.690
Speaking of February...

00:17:09.690 --> 00:17:12.530
Higashida, Valentine's Day
is this month, right?

00:17:12.780 --> 00:17:15.740
Actually, the anniversary
of the death of St. Valentine.

00:17:15.950 --> 00:17:17.280
So...

00:17:18.620 --> 00:17:20.200
eat my chocolate!

00:17:20.200 --> 00:17:22.910
You don't need
to sympathize with me.

00:17:23.290 --> 00:17:24.750
That's not it, Higashida!

00:17:25.000 --> 00:17:28.380
It's not about "obligation chocolate"
or "chocolate for that special someone."

00:17:29.300 --> 00:17:30.340
Anyway...

00:17:31.170 --> 00:17:33.720
please eat the chocolate I make.

00:17:35.260 --> 00:17:38.260
Promise me! A pinky swear!

00:17:38.260 --> 00:17:39.720
Miyakoshi...

00:17:39.720 --> 00:17:42.680
why would you make
something for me?

00:17:43.770 --> 00:17:45.400
I heard.

00:17:46.060 --> 00:17:48.650
You're the one this year, huh?

00:17:49.980 --> 00:17:52.400
The one in charge of eating
Miyakoshi's chocolate.

00:17:52.400 --> 00:17:53.320
In charge of?

00:17:53.650 --> 00:17:54.900
Good.

00:17:55.160 --> 00:17:58.070
I'm glad she chose you,
someone who can't say no.

00:17:58.620 --> 00:18:00.580
It was me last year.

00:18:01.080 --> 00:18:02.540
I lost at rock paper scissors.

00:18:02.910 --> 00:18:04.540
Please wait a moment, Muranushi.

00:18:05.170 --> 00:18:08.500
Does something happen
if you eat Miyakoshi's chocolate?

00:18:09.460 --> 00:18:10.630
You could say that.

00:18:10.880 --> 00:18:12.710
For example...

00:18:14.130 --> 00:18:18.720
St. Valentine himself comes down
from the heavens.

00:18:20.390 --> 00:18:21.770
That's what it tastes like.

00:18:25.100 --> 00:18:26.900
Was it a near-death experience?

00:18:31.980 --> 00:18:33.530
The 14th at last...

00:18:34.360 --> 00:18:37.570
This may be the most tension
I've ever felt on Valentine's Day.

00:18:45.540 --> 00:18:46.410
Um...

00:18:47.040 --> 00:18:50.880
Would you accept this, Higashida?

00:18:51.380 --> 00:18:52.880
<i>Scary!</i>

00:18:54.210 --> 00:18:57.510
<i>In the end, I let her give it to me.</i>

00:18:59.140 --> 00:19:00.890
<i>Shindou sure is popular
with the ladies.</i>

00:18:59.300 --> 00:19:00.890
I wanted to see you!

00:19:01.140 --> 00:19:02.310
Here, Yuuta.

00:19:02.510 --> 00:19:04.390
You're not working
at the club tonight, right?

00:19:04.390 --> 00:19:05.480
We brought our gifts here.

00:19:05.480 --> 00:19:07.390
Thank you, ladies!

00:19:08.350 --> 00:19:09.980
His customers from the host club...

00:19:10.810 --> 00:19:13.190
I'm so happy!
Another bonanza this year!

00:19:13.690 --> 00:19:15.820
I'll be able to live
a good long while on this.

00:19:16.150 --> 00:19:17.150
Yuuta...

00:19:19.160 --> 00:19:20.410
Happy Valentine's Day!

00:19:21.030 --> 00:19:22.530
I've got something for you, too.

00:19:23.660 --> 00:19:24.580
But...

00:19:24.830 --> 00:19:25.950
that's cash.

00:19:26.450 --> 00:19:29.540
Take the money and go to the chocolate
section in a department store.

00:19:29.540 --> 00:19:32.710
Then get the most expensive chocolate
and give the money to the clerk.

00:19:32.710 --> 00:19:36.260
Say, "This is for my honey,
so do a nice job wrapping it."

00:19:36.630 --> 00:19:39.220
If you buy it and bring it back,
I'll let you keep the change.

00:19:40.340 --> 00:19:41.300
The change...

00:19:41.800 --> 00:19:44.220
If you want the chocolate,
you can keep that, too.

00:19:49.850 --> 00:19:52.560
Um, Miyakoshi...
About the chocolate—

00:19:52.560 --> 00:19:55.110
Eat it. Don't throw it away.
You'd better eat it.

00:19:56.110 --> 00:19:57.690
That's not what I wanted to say.

00:19:58.030 --> 00:20:01.160
Didn't you have anyone else
you wanted to give it to?

00:20:01.780 --> 00:20:03.160
Like a person you're interested in?

00:20:03.410 --> 00:20:05.740
You didn't have to give it to me.

00:20:07.330 --> 00:20:10.120
If I gave it to that person,
would they eat it?

00:20:10.540 --> 00:20:12.250
I'm sure they would!

00:20:12.250 --> 00:20:13.840
After all, you're cute.

00:20:14.290 --> 00:20:15.590
<i>When you keep your mouth shut.</i>

00:20:17.420 --> 00:20:18.090
Okay, then...

00:20:18.880 --> 00:20:20.090
I love you, Higashida!

00:20:20.090 --> 00:20:21.430
Cut it out, Miyakoshi!

00:20:25.060 --> 00:20:27.140
Just shut up and eat it!

00:20:28.020 --> 00:20:30.310
It looks tasty enough.

00:20:30.310 --> 00:20:31.270
That's true.

00:20:31.560 --> 00:20:33.270
It's fine! I think!

00:20:34.980 --> 00:20:36.110
All right, just one.

00:20:49.750 --> 00:20:50.500
HACK

00:21:08.720 --> 00:21:10.100
<i>Higashida...</i>

00:21:10.520 --> 00:21:12.020
<i>Higashida...</i>

00:21:12.850 --> 00:21:14.350
<i>Higashida...</i>

00:21:14.600 --> 00:21:16.230
<i>Higashida...</i>

00:21:16.520 --> 00:21:19.480
<i>Love and peace!</i>

00:21:20.860 --> 00:21:23.860
S-Saint Valentine!

00:21:24.950 --> 00:21:26.240
Down from the heavens.

00:21:26.700 --> 00:21:28.790
And he said my name.

00:21:32.160 --> 00:21:34.830
Sorry, Higashida.
I'll throw these out.

00:21:37.130 --> 00:21:39.800
N-No. Miyakoshi...

00:21:40.510 --> 00:21:43.840
You went to the trouble
of making it for me...

00:21:44.680 --> 00:21:47.050
You know, love and peace...

00:21:47.350 --> 00:21:49.970
I'll take it home.

00:21:49.970 --> 00:21:51.850
H-Higashida!

00:21:52.230 --> 00:21:53.390
You're a hero.

00:21:53.640 --> 00:21:55.190
You're a hero, Higashida!

00:23:26.030 --> 00:23:36.040
NEXT EPISODE PREVIEW

00:23:26.280 --> 00:23:27.860
And so, I started working.

00:23:27.860 --> 00:23:29.530
Apparently, the story
is about me next time!

00:23:29.530 --> 00:23:33.240
Yes. If there are rapid changes, hopefully
it's in the weather and not the story.

00:23:33.120 --> 00:23:36.040
LIFE ISN'T THAT EASY

00:23:33.240 --> 00:23:36.040
Next time, "Life isn't That Easy."
